    "['ssh user [parameter1] authentication-type [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': \"username client001 secret @%@%.OuC6Vo7Z,A'y~/KB&,vmd@%@%\", 'parent_command': [], 'root': \"username client001 secret @%@%.OuC6Vo7Z,A'y~/KB&,vmd@%@%\", 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##  \\nusername client001 secret @%@%.OuC6Vo7Z,A'y~/KB&,vmd@%@%  \\nip ssh password-authentication  \\n##  \\n\\n**Note:**  \\n1. The Cisco equivalent combines the username/password creation (`username client001 secret`) and enables SSH password authentication globally (`ip ssh password-authentication`), as Cisco doesn't have a per-user SSH authentication-type command like Huawei.  \\n2. The cipher password from Huawei's config would need to be replaced with the actual plaintext password (or a new Cisco-compatible hash) in a real deployment, as Cisco doesn't share Huawei's cipher format.  \\n3. Additional SSH server configuration (like enabling SSH) would be required on Cisco for full equivalence.\", 'trans_template': \"username client001 secret @%@%.OuC6Vo7Z,A'y~/KB&,vmd@%@%\"}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ip ssh password-authentication', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'ip ssh password-authentication', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##  \\nusername client001 secret @%@%.OuC6Vo7Z,A'y~/KB&,vmd@%@%  \\nip ssh password-authentication  \\n##  \\n\\n**Note:**  \\n1. The Cisco equivalent combines the username/password creation (`username client001 secret`) and enables SSH password authentication globally (`ip ssh password-authentication`), as Cisco doesn't have a per-user SSH authentication-type command like Huawei.  \\n2. The cipher password from Huawei's config would need to be replaced with the actual plaintext password (or a new Cisco-compatible hash) in a real deployment, as Cisco doesn't share Huawei's cipher format.  \\n3. Additional SSH server configuration (like enabling SSH) would be required on Cisco for full equivalence.\", 'trans_template': 'ip ssh password-authentication'}]]": 1,
